```python
def is_palindrome(s):
    s = ''.join(ch.lower() for ch in s if ch.isalnum())
    if len(s) <= 1:
        return True
    if s[0] != s[-1]:
        return False
    return is_palindrome(s[1:-1])
```
Base cases: empty string or single character -> True. First and last characters differ -> False. Recursive step: check substring without first and last characters. A poor answer (e.g., using a loop, or not handling case/non-alphanumeric) reveals inability to translate a string problem into a recursive reduction and handle preprocessing.
